[Music]  in southern texas just a few miles from  the mexico border and almost three hours  from san antonio sits the quiet town of  del rio  texas is a place where local politics  are often steeped in anti-lgbt rhetoric  but in a wave of change del rio elected  its first openly gay mayor in 2018.  i'm zoe saldana from bc and i'm teaming  up a great big story to shine a light on  american latinx excellence around the  country  i'm bruno lozano and i'm the mayor of  del rio texas  i was born and raised here in dario  texas  i joined the military when i was 21  i served in the air force under don't  ask hotel  i laughed and lived in big cities  and i came back to del rio texas in  2016.  [Music]  i was not openly gay until maybe i was  15 years old  growing up i was bullied because i was  flamboyant i was feminine i was more  feminine and being feminine is  considered a weakness in the machismo  culture that permeates this entire area  but the same people who bullied me voted  me into office  bruno ran on a platform built on  infrastructure employment and tourism  despite running against an incumbent  bruno won his election with 62 percent  of the vote  i decided to run for office because i've  always believed in del rio and his full  potential  on my campaign trail i did not run as a  gay politician or as a gay mayor i ran  as bruno who happens to be all of these  other things miss carpenter you may now  have the floor to speak for three  minutes  you can win people's hearts over as long  as you are true to yourself and true to  your mind and goal  [Music]  since becoming mayor bruno has written  support resolutions for local  initiatives appointed members of the  parks committee and housing authority  but most importantly he has created a  space for people like him  for me the future of del rio is being a  place where people are welcome are  inviting and are different  i left looking for acceptance and  looking for people like me but i chose  to come back to del rio because my  community is here and it's important for  people who are different like myself to  be visible  you can be gay you can be different and  you can still run for office here in del  rio texas and win an election  [Music]  you

